What:		/proc/sentry_reporter/oom
Date:		February 2025
Contact:	Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd. <sxt1001@huawei.com>
Description:
		Control OOM (Out Of Memory) event reporting functionality.

		Write Values:
			"on"  - Enable OOM event reporting
			"off" - Disable OOM event reporting

		Read Values:
			"on" or "off" - Current OOM event reporting status

		Examples:
			# Enable OOM event reporting
			echo "on" > /proc/sentry_reporter/oom

			# Disable OOM event reporting
			echo "off" > /proc/sentry_reporter/oom

			# Check current status
			cat /proc/sentry_reporter/oom
			on

		Function Details:
		- Monitors system low memory events
		- Supports both synchronous and asynchronous reclaim modes
		- Configurable timeout (via module parameter oom_timeout_ms)

What:		/proc/sentry_reporter/power_off
Date:		February 2025
Contact:	Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd. <sxt1001@huawei.com>
Description:
		Control power off event reporting functionality.

		Write Values:
			"on"  - Enable power off event reporting
			"off" - Disable power off event reporting

		Read Values:
			"on" or "off" - Current power off event reporting status

		Examples:
			# Enable power off event reporting
			echo "on" > /proc/sentry_reporter/power_off

			# Disable power off event reporting
			echo "off" > /proc/sentry_reporter/power_off

			# Check current status
			cat /proc/sentry_reporter/power_off
			on

		Function Details:
		- Listens for ACPI power button events (e.g. comes from BMC power off event)
		- Sends notifications before system shutdown
		- Intercepts ACPI power button events and requires UBPRM response
		- Without UBPRM support, ACPI power button events becomes unavailable
		- Only enable in UB environments with active UBPRM
		- Configurable timeout (via module parameter reboot_timeout_ms)

